Do not replace the domain with `contoso.local`; the current project domain is `contoso.com`.

## Lab configuration

Edit the configuration at the beginning of `V1.ps1` for another environment:


The OU and group values are intentionally placeholders until the environment details are gathered. The script will not guess an OU.

## Reports


The access audit is read-only. It does not disable accounts, remove groups, delete users, or change audited employees.

## Requirements

Run from a management host with the ActiveDirectory module and appropriate permissions. The account creation path requires a secure temporary password. Use `-DryRun` to validate data and display planned account actions without creating the account.

## Future cloud expansion

Entra ID and Azure Virtual Desktop are intentionally future work. A later Power Automate or Azure Automation step can use Microsoft Graph or Az modules after approved authentication, subscriptions, host pools, images, networking, licensing, and RBAC are available. This project does not pretend those cloud resources are configured.

This project processes one Workday-style employee record at a time and performs a controlled Active Directory onboarding workflow.

`Workday CSV or JSON -> Validation -> LON-DC1 check -> Department-based OU -> Duplicate check -> AD account -> Read-only audit -> Reports and logs`

## Project files

- `V2.ps1`: Main working PowerShell onboarding script.
- `V2.Present.ps1`: Presentation copy with beginner-friendly comments. Its executable PowerShell code matches `V2.ps1`.
- `V1.ps1`: Earlier project version retained for reference.

